WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.869
-My first guest is a Golden
Globe and Grammy-nominated

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.738
artist and actor who you can see
as a coach on "The Voice,"

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.707
which airs Mondays and Tuesdays
on NBC.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:11.678
And you can see him in
the new movie "Chaos Walking,"

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.212
which is in theaters Friday.

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.314
Here is Nick Jonas.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.450
Yeah!
-Yay!

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.452
-You were fantastic, buddy.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.487
You were fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.923
-I watched from home.
I was, like, rooting for you.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.125
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:28.327
The video was my fave.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.296
I love the tonal sketch.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.500
And I love the two new jams,
the two new songs.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.402
"Spaceman" is -- I loved.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:39.939
I didn't hear --
I didn't know the other new one.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.574
-It hasn't been released yet.
That's what I'm saying.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.908
I kind of mentioned it
in the monologue,

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:45.444
but I was thinking it's been
a full year to the day,

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:48.581
the exact day,
since my last live performance.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.483
So, I was just like, "Let's just
keep it really simple --

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.553
host and be a musical guest
and premiere two new songs."

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.821
I mean, why not?

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.556
-Did you get nervous
coming down the steps?

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.024
I thought that's always one of
my most nerve-racking moments.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:03.229
-Yeah, so, I guess
one of the newest traditions

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.965
is the hosts writing a note
to each other.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:09.301
-Really?
-Which I had just become hip to

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:12.805
'cause I saw Regina King
post about it.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.575
And then Regé-Jean posted that

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.976
they had each written a note
to each other.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.978
And so, you know,
I wrote mine to Maya Rudolph,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.980
who just got announced
as the next host.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.283
And then, what they do is, they
take it from your dressing room

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.185
and put it right on the door
before you walk out.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:27.620
So you've got, you know,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.055
all these cool notes
from all the other hosts,

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.223
and the last,
I think, six, seven hosts

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.792
just wishing each other
good luck,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.694
but it feels like a mutual --
sort of, like,

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.029
"Hey, take a deep breath.
Don't trip down the stairs.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:39.164
Take your time on the monologue
and do your thing."

00:01:39.164 --> 00:01:41.100
It was really special.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.970
-Here's the vinyl right here.
This is the --

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.838
March 12th, it comes out.
-Mm.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:48.007
-"Spaceman."
Where did you shoot this?

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.809
I'm assuming -- I know you.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.911
Did you go to space?
Were you on Mars?

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.513
-We went to Mars.
-Yeah, I figured.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.581
-Yeah, Elon Musk
funded the whole thing.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:55.881
-I knew it.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.784
-It was the most expensive
album photo shoot ever.

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.953
-And with COVID and everything,
can you imagine?

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:04.557
-Yeah, I think it was just
an extra wealthy shoot.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:08.494
But, basically,
we went out to Barstow.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.830
Apparently, there was a volcano
there at one point.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.765
And now
there's this volcanic rock --

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.667
it's like a crater --

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.403
which, you know,
is both really cool,

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.105
but, also, very dangerous.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:22.809
I still have battle scars
from all over my hands

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.578
from falling and shredding
my hands on this volcanic rock.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.746
-I mean, that lava.
-It looked really cool, so...

00:02:27.746 --> 00:02:29.048
-No, the coolest shot.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.316
-...I don't really care,
you know?

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.619
You know, I sort of
started writing this record

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.388
back in July.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.057
My wife was over in Germany,

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.559
finishing up this little movie
called "The Matrix."

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:41.660
And...
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.062
And I was like, "You know,

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.832
I feel very disconnected
from the world, first of all,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.568
and now my person."
-Yeah.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:52.171
-And I just dug in writing it
with Greg Kurstin and Mozella.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.472
Within a couple of days,

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.574
I was like, "Oh, this is --
this is a solo album."

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.009
Then a few days later,
I was like,

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.845
"This is a --
a kind of like themed album."

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.047
You know, giving --

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.282
This idea that
we've all had this year now --

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.617
I loved the thing with John,
by the way.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.052
It was great.
-Ah.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.421
-But this year of being sort of
disconnected from reality,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.555
disconnected from the world,

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.490
and feeling like
we're on our own planet.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.826
And, you know, also,

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.527
obviously missing her
at that time, as well,

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:17.262
and then reconnecting with her.

00:03:17.262 --> 00:03:19.732
And then the main theme
from this album, I think,

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.900
is, more than anything,

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.435
is just about hopefulness
for the future

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:25.104
and seeing a brighter day ahead.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.807
-Ah, we need that now,
more than ever, buddy.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.375
I wanted to ask you
about something

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:32.578
that you called
the Jonas Blessing.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:33.980
Now, can --
-Mm.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.514
-...can you --
can you first explain

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.984
to everyone what it is --
who don't know?

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.252
-Sure. I'd be happy to.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.619
I mean, it's quite simple,
you know?

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.055
In reality,
what happened is that,

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.457
when the brothers
got back together --

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.858
we went on tour
on the Happiness Begins Tour

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.793
back in 2019 --

00:03:47.793 --> 00:03:51.463
we had a number of athletes,
high-performing athletes,

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.132
come out to see shows.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.068
So, the first was
Cody Bellinger,

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:57.470
who then went on to win

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.072
the World Series
with the Dodgers, right?

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.540
-Amazing.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:05.577
-We had Patrick Mahomes,
who, in the 2020 Super Bowl,

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.446
won the Super Bowl
with the Kansas City Chiefs.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.348
-Wow.
-He came to a show in K.C.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:13.186
And then Lewis Hamilton, who
surpassed the all-time record...

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:15.655
-Oh, yeah.
-He went on to,

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.357
after he came to a show,
to do that.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:21.193
So, basically, we established,
and I think it was really me

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:22.761
more than the brothers --
I saw the trend.

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.096
I was saying...
-You think?

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.565
-..."We're gonna have to start
charging these athletes.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:28.801
If they want the Jonas Blessing,
to come to a show

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.770
and then
go on to win a championship,

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.171
they're gonna have to pay up."
-Yeah.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.406
-You know?
-Yeah.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.241
You think that it was you
that came up with it,

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.609
but it might have been --
it might have been someone else?

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.044
-Yeah.
Little known fact, too, Jimmy,

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:40.746
is that Tom Brady --

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:43.883
we actually did a private,
COVID-safe show for Tom Brady

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:45.651
before the Super Bowl,
and that's why.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.120
-[ Laughs ] There you go.
That's a -- That's a juicy --

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.922
That's the story
I'm talking about.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.658
That's what I -- That's what I
wanted to get to, of course.

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:55.928
I want to talk about
your new movie, "Chaos Walking."

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.429
Tell us every--
-Yes.

00:04:57.429 --> 00:05:00.533
-Tell everyone what this
is about and who you play.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.934
It's a good -- great cast.
-Well, you know, I was happy

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.837
to give these other actors,
these scrubs, these newbies

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.040
a shot in this movie.
-Oh.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.975
-Tom Holland, Daisy Ridley.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.810
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.
-You know, Mads Mikkelsen.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.845
No one's ever heard of them.
Cynthia Erivo.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.980
So, yeah. I don't know.
I was just happy to be there.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.450
With a cast like that,
it was -- it was unbelievable.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:21.053
-Doug Liman directing.
-Doug Liman directing --

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.087
the legend that he is.

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:23.923
It's a -- It's a wild ride,
you know?

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:28.661
It's a dystopian world where
there's this settlement of men

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:31.230
who --
basically, something happened.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.498
I don't want
to give too much away.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.768
But all of their thoughts
and visions in their head

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.803
are heard and seen
in an orb around them.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.973
So, as you can imagine,
that creates some problems.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:43.342
-I want to --
I also want to talk about --

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:45.344
you returned as a coach on
"The Voice,"

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.046
and people love this.

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.315
This is your second season
as a coach.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.350
And I have a theory already.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.652
I feel like, the first season,

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:55.922
I think they gave you
a good kind of ribbing.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.623
They kind of --
They kind of said, like,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.191
"Oh, this newbie, this guy."

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:00.426
And then...
-Yeah.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.860
-And now you're back,
and you're like,

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.495
"I know --
I know how to play this game.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:04.597
Let's go.
You want to go, Blake?"

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.399
-Well, that's the thing.
That first year

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:08.567
definitely is like
you're the new kid at school.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:09.701
You know?
-Yeah.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.670
-But I came out swinging
this time.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:12.838
You know, I was like,

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:14.506
"I'm not gonna feel things out."
-Yeah.

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:15.908
-"I'm gonna go
straight for the jugular."

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.943
-Good.
-And it was --

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:19.478
first day of blind auditions,

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:20.779
which actually aired
last night...

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:22.081
-It was great.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.117
-The second night is tonight,
probably just aired.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:27.820
...is --
you know, it's a lot of fun.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.890
It's like Kelly is
the three of our, like, sister.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.792
And we're all, you know,
just having fun

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:37.129
and giving each other
the necessary amount of crap.

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:38.397
And...
-Yeah.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:40.967
-You know, I'm just trying
to keep Blake humble.

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.768
-[ Chuckles ] How --
-You know, he's won seven times,

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.370
he thinks that he's
the Tom Brady of "The Voice,"

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:46.905
and he needs to calm down.

00:06:46.905 --> 00:06:49.074
-[ Chuckles ]
You'll never do it.

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:51.010
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.379
Here's Nick Jonas in
the new season of "The Voice."

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.680
Take a look at this.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.881
-I didn't know you got blocked.

00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:57.049
I didn't even realize
you got blocked.

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.651
-Nor did I.
-You see what he's done, Nick?

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.086
When Kelly blocked Blake...
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:04.122
-...he set you up making
you think that he was here

00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:05.624
looking out for your interests.

00:07:05.624 --> 00:07:06.992
-Wait. Unless you did it.

00:07:06.992 --> 00:07:08.894
-It can only be the person
that went before you, Nick.

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:10.429
-Yes. Okay. So it was you.
-No, that's not true!

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:11.897
That's not -- That --
I didn't -- What?!

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:13.466
-Do you want to be
on a liar's team?

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:15.501
-Blake always lies about it,
too.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.069
-If I did, it was an accident.

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.604
I was trying to --
I was trying to --

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:19.972
-Oh, my gosh!
-Unbelievable.

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.440
-"It was an accident."
-"If I did..."

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.975
-He could have picked any of us
to block.

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.044
-He must be that afraid
of me as a coach.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:26.045
-Who did he pick?

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:27.379
-Nick Jonas, everybody.

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:29.281
"The Voice" --
blind auditions continue

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:33.785
next Monday at 8:00
and Tuesday at 9:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:07:33.785 --> 00:07:35.521
Nick, we always ask you
to do something

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.989
and play a game or something.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:40.359
Do you -- Would you mind?
-I would love to.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.995
I was actually thinking,
"This interview is so boring.

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.363
Let's just play a game already."

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.899
-More with Nick Jonas
when we come back. Stick around.

